# Expenses domain (budget, expenses, receipts, reports, reporting,
# statistics). The domain is split into suites, one per slice:
#   expenses-stats, expenses-budgeting(-writes), expenses-core,
#   expenses-reporting(-create), expenses-import-upload, expenses-import,
#   and this file (GET /v1/reports/overview).
# parity/expenses-run.sh seeds every fixture and runs all of them in order:
#   parity/expenses-run.sh http://127.0.0.1:8081 http://127.0.0.1:18112
#
# This file alone: load parity/expenses-core-setup.sql, then
# parity/expenses-setup.sql, then
#   go run ./cmd/parity -a http://127.0.0.1:8081 -b http://127.0.0.1:18112 -jwt-secret parity-secret \
#     -cases parity/expenses.jsonl -ignore requestId,generatedAt
